    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about it being the mind, but it doesn't feel like \"creations.\" they feel like specific, heavy moments. i remember the smell of old parchment, the weight of a specific kind of wax seal, and this constant, underlying pressure to maintain a certain level of decorum even when everything was falling apart politically. it was around the time of the revolution, i think. \n\ninstead of the big names like napoleon, can we look at the actual diplomats and advisors? the people who were in the rooms making the decisions, not just the ones in the history books for being famous. maybe someone who was more of a strategist or a negotiator. i want to see if there's someone whose specific temperament or situation matches this \"pressure\" i keep feeling.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
